     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Estrogen-progestin oral contraceptives block the ovulatory surge of sex steroids; most effective = drospirenone + ethinyl estradiol w a shorter (4-day) hormone-free interval. Risk of VTE may be higher w drospirenone."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Progesterone vaginal suppository 200-400 mg Q1x day, micronized progesterone 100 mg @ bedtime for 10-12 days b4 menses, or medroxyprogesterone 200 mg IM Q2-3 months."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Rarely, for very severe or refractory Sx: a GnRH agonist (eg, leuprolide 3.75 mg IM or goserelin 3.6 mg SC monthly) w ↓dose estrogen/progestin."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Fluid retention may be relieved by reducing sodium and taking a diuretic (eg, spironolactone 100 mg orally Q1x day) just b4 Sx are expected."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Calcium 600 mg twice a day may lessen (−) mood and somatic Sx; chasteberry, vit B6 (⍉more than 100 mg/day) and vit E are mildly effective."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
